"proposal": {
    "capability": "deployment.set-probes",
    "target": {"group": "apps", "kind": "Deployment", "namespace": "payments", "name": "payments-worker", "uid": "uid-deployment-payments-worker"},
    "params": {
        "container": "app",
        "liveness": {
            "timeoutSeconds": 10
        }
    },
    "expected_effect": "Allow the application more time to respond to liveness probes during startup, preventing premature restarts.",
    "rationale": "The liveness probe timeout (2s) is too short compared to the application's startup time (46s). Increasing the timeout to 10s would give the application sufficient time to initialize before the probe fails. This aligns with the evidence showing the application was killed during startup due to probe failures. The probe timeout is the most likely cause, as the application's logs (not yet examined) would show it starting but not responding to probes quickly enough. Adjusting the timeout to match the observed startup time would resolve the issue without changing other probe parameters, which are in",
